{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And I will break the pride of your strength.</b> Corresponding to ״ואשבור מוטות עולכם״ (Lev. 26:12-13's promise to break the bars of their yoke) — and it is the first. Your heaven like iron — corresponding to ״ונתתי גשמיכם״ (the promise to give your rains) — and it is the second." "<b>Your land like copper.</b> Corresponding to ״בעתם״ (the promise that the land would yield its produce in its time) — and it is a blessing in its own right — and it is the third." "<b>Like copper (כנחשה).</b> A noun form of copper, like ״ונחתה קשת נחושה זרועותי״."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:15:33.045155516Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}